From d6bba6f10ad2b66518f4682dd6c277731535f8e7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Julian Greilich <j.greilich@gmx.de>
Date: Tue, 11 Nov 2025 09:55:28 +0100
Subject: a11y Android: Use TYPE_WINDOW_CONTENT_CHANGED for all value changes

* The correct way to announce changes of accessible name, description
  and value is to use the EventType TYPE_WINDOW_CONTENT_CHANGED (with
  the corresponding CONTENT_CHANGE_TYPE) instead of TYPE_ANNOUNCEMENT.
* When TYPE_ANNOUNCEMENT was used, multiple changes were all announced
  after another, even when the element was not visible anymore,
  while now only the last change is announced.
* This is also a more general solution to the problem solved with
  a067a4f6dade4c53303459469917c94ef6268941, which only solved this
  for the ProgressBar.
* We don't need to pass the (new) value to the
  notifyValueChanged and notifyNameOrDescriptionChanged method anymore.

Fixes: QTBUG-150377
Task-number: QTBUG-139712
Pick-to: 6.12 6.8
Change-Id: I3917ae5d2a17c6e470d499b364d6a0456c9d3601
Reviewed-by: Assam Boudjelthia <assam.boudjelthia@qt.io>
(cherry picked from commit e1b83898a7920db9c25dfa11e6aafb6bd0206d85)
